WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.825
Multilingual language models must decide how much
to train on each language,

00:00:04.905 --> 00:00:08.697
and the standard answer has been temperature-based
sampling.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:11.923
This paper from Google Research introduces UniMax,

00:00:12.003 --> 00:00:17.731
a simple sampling method that gives more uniform
coverage to high-resource languages while

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:22.830
explicitly capping how many times any low-resource
language's data is repeated.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.670
Across many benchmarks and model scales, UniMax
beats temperature sampling,

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.057
and the gains persist as models grow.

00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:37.672
The authors also release a refreshed mC4 corpus of
twenty-nine trillion characters across one hundred seven languages,

00:00:37.752 --> 00:00:40.770
along with umT5 checkpoints trained with UniMax.
